    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0322" n="202" xml:id="pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-16T22:00:00-06:00">December 16, 1931—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 17—12:08 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>121. Your 69, December 16, 7 p.m. Mexican Minister informs me that in accordance
                    with the Estrada doctrine<anchor n="27" xml:id="d228-f1"/> relations between
                    Mexico and El Salvador have not been interrupted but that he has taken no action
                    beyond acknowledging receipt of a note informing him of the change of
                    government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d228-f1" n="27" xml:id="d228-f1-content">
                <p>Institute Americano de Derecho y Legislacion Comparada, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >La Doctrina Estrada</hi> (Mexico, Publicaciones del Institute Americano de
                    Derecho y Legislacion Comparada, 1930), and <hi rendition="#italic">La Opinion
                        Universal sobre La Doctrina Estrada</hi>, etc. (Mexico, Publicaciones del
                    Institute Americano de Derecho y Legislacion Comparada, 1931).</p>
            </note>
